@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium profile diagram — a domain profile with four stereotypes extending different metaclasses, tagged values, and stereotype inheritance.
'   usecase:      Teach multiple stereotypes, tagged values, inheritance between stereotypes, and extending different metaclasses.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       Enterprise / SOA
' ============================================================================
title Example Profile Diagram - Medium Domain Profile

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' "EnterpriseProfile" defines four stereotypes for SOA modelling:
'   «Service»       extends Component
'   «RESTEndpoint»  extends Class
'   «Entity»        extends Class
'   «ValueObject»   extends Class
' Plus a stereotype GENERALIZATION: «ValueObject» is a kind of «Entity»
# (specialised stereotype inherits its parent's tagged values).
' Each stereotype carries tagged values shown as stereotype-scope attributes.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

package "EnterpriseProfile" <<profile>> {

  ' --- Metaclasses ------------------------------------------------------
  class Component << (M,#B4A7E5) metaclass >> { }
  class Class     << (M,#B4A7E5) metaclass >> { }

  ' --- Stereotypes ------------------------------------------------------
  class Service << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + endpoint : String
    + version  : String
  }

  class RESTEndpoint << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + method : HTTPMethod
    + path   : String
  }

  class Entity << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + tableName : String
  }

  class ValueObject << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + immutable : Boolean
  }

  ' --- Extensions (stereotype -> metaclass) -----------------------------
  Service      ..> Component : <<extend>>
  RESTEndpoint ..> Class     : <<extend>>
  Entity       ..> Class     : <<extend>>
  ValueObject  ..> Class     : <<extend>>

  ' --- Stereotype generalization ----------------------------------------
  ' ValueObject SPECIALISES Entity — it inherits tableName and adds
  ' immutable.  Drawn with the hollow-triangle generalization arrow.
  ValueObject --|> Entity
}

note right of Service
  <b>Stereotype generalization</b>
  ValueObject --|> Entity
  means «ValueObject» inherits the
  tableName tagged value from
  «Entity» and adds its own
  immutable flag.  The base element
  type is still Class.
end note

note bottom of RESTEndpoint
  <b>Different metaclasses</b>
  Service extends Component; the
  others extend Class.  A stereotype
  must name exactly which metaclass
  it extends, because the tagged
  values only become applicable on
  elements of THAT metaclass.
end note

@enduml
